🌐 Supply Chain Builder — Day 30 of #60DaysOfClaudeAI
An interactive, single-file web app that teaches supply chain fundamentals through hands-on decision-making — built for complete beginners.
🎯 What It Does
Welcome Screen — introduces what a supply chain is in plain English.
Random Company Generator — creates a new company each playthrough with a random industry, products, countries served, and demand level.
5 Guided Decisions — for each one, the app explains the concept, why it matters, and the trade-offs before you choose:
Number of suppliers (single vs. multiple)
Factory location (local / offshore / hybrid)
Warehouse strategy (central / regional / none)
Transportation method (road / rail / sea / air)
Inventory strategy (low / balanced / high)
Live Metrics Dashboard — Cost, Delivery Speed, Risk, Customer Satisfaction, and Sustainability update with animated progress bars after every choice.
Final Report — an Overall Supply Chain Score (0–100), strengths, weaknesses, biggest risk, and three practical improvement recommendations.
Replay — generate a brand-new random company and start over.
🛠️ Tech Stack
React 18 (via CDN)
Babel Standalone (JSX in-browser, no build step)
Plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript
Single .html file — no npm, no backend, no external assets
100% offline — just open the file in any browser
🎨 Design
Dark, premium enterprise dashboard aesthetic
Rounded cards with hover effects and smooth transitions
Animated progress bars for all metrics
Fully responsive layout
▶️ How to Run
Download supply-chain-builder.html and open it directly in any modern browser. No installation required.
📚 Why This Project
Part of my #60DaysOfClaudeAI challenge — building one polished, single-file web app every day. Day 30 focuses on making an abstract business concept (supply chain management) tangible and understandable through interactive simulation.
